WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:07.320
A new Iron person, a possible secret villain,&nbsp;
and Namor earning his wings. What other secrets&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:10.939
are hiding in the new trailer for&nbsp;
"Black Panther: Wakanda Forever?"

00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:16.380
56 seconds into the trailer, we get a great&nbsp;
look at Namor in all his winged-foot glory.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:21.420
He's introduced via a voiceover from&nbsp;
M'Baku and will supposedly serve as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:26.160
the film's primary antagonist. Marvel&nbsp;
Studios decided to give the character a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:31.800
Mayan spin for his MCU introduction. Namor's&nbsp;
updated look for the MCU looks incredible,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:36.900
and the inclusion of his winged feet is enough&nbsp;
to get any fans of the Sub-Mariner excited.

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:45.834
"They don't call him general or king, they&nbsp;
call him K'uk'ulkan, the feather serpent god."

00:00:45.834 --> 00:00:50.460
The trailer also makes it clear that killing&nbsp;
him would risk eternal war. In the comics,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:53.460
Wakanda and Atlantis almost never see eye-to-eye,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:57.180
and it looks like "Wakanda Forever"&nbsp;
perfectly sets up that relationship.

00:00:57.180 --> 00:01:05.100
Marvel Comics introduced Namor in 1939 in "Marvel&nbsp;
Comics #1" from then-publisher Timely Comics. He&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:10.440
is the son of an Atlantean princess, although&nbsp;
due to his human father, he doesn't share the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:16.020
same blue-tinted skin as most Atlanteans. In the&nbsp;
comics, he's also usually the King of Atlantis,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:22.680
though his MCU debut will include some changes&nbsp;
according to Namor actor Tenoch Huerta. His powers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:28.260
include underwater breathing, superhuman strength,&nbsp;
and the ability to fly using the wings on his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:33.780
feet. Because of his first publication date, he&nbsp;
is sometimes considered Marvel's first mutant.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:39.813
Interestingly, Huerta confirmed to Empire that&nbsp;
the character is a mutant in "Wakanda Forever."

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:44.760
Namor isn't the only new comic&nbsp;
character popping up in Wakanda Forever;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:49.500
in a quick shot in the trailer for "Black&nbsp;
Panther: Wakanda Forever," viewers can see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:53.760
none other than Riri Williams, who&nbsp;
in the comics is known as Ironheart.

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:59.280
This is a fitting character to be introduced in&nbsp;
"Black Panther: Wakanda Forever," considering&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:02.880
that the mantle of Black Panther has&nbsp;
also changed hands. In the comics,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:07.440
Williams is a genius-level intellect&nbsp;
by age five. She crafts her own Iron&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:12.360
Man suit after reverse engineering pieces&nbsp;
from an Iron Man armor design. Chances are,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:16.680
Williams is constructing her own armor suit&nbsp;
from whatever Tony Stark armor she's been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.680 --> 00:02:21.180
able to find – which shouldn't be too hard, since&nbsp;
it's not like he's been super careful with them.

00:02:21.180 --> 00:02:24.720
By the end of the trailer, we see&nbsp;
Williams' Ironheart persona in flight,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:30.238
so it doesn't look like it will take her long&nbsp;
to step up to the proverbial Iron Man plate.

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:35.700
We get a small glimpse at Attuma in the first&nbsp;
teaser for "Black Panther: Wakanda Forever,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:40.680
where he appears on a bridge ready to fight what&nbsp;
looks to be Okoye. We're getting a better look&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:45.480
at that moment in the trailer, where the villain&nbsp;
launches himself into the air before slamming down&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:51.240
on the bridge. Attuma's inclusion in the Phase&nbsp;
4 film is very important, as the character is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.240 --> 00:02:56.580
the archnemesis of Namor in the comics. We fully&nbsp;
expect to see a battle for power between the two.

00:02:56.580 --> 00:03:02.100
The history between Namor and Attuma is lengthy,&nbsp;
and there are any number of stories we could see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:07.080
adapted into the new movie. With Namor being&nbsp;
more of an anti-hero than an outright villain,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:10.920
we might see Attuma play a little more&nbsp;
of the bad guy role than his nemesis&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:15.540
counterpart. Attuma plans to flood the&nbsp;
surface world in the comics, and since we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:21.418
see Wakanda getting flushed out in the teaser,&nbsp;
perhaps it was all his doing and not Namor's.

00:03:21.780 --> 00:03:26.340
And finally, we get a "Black Panther"&nbsp;
throwback in the trailer's final moment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.340 --> 00:03:29.640
when the new mantle wearer does&nbsp;
their superhero landing from high&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:34.440
above. While it's not fully confirmed in the&nbsp;
preview who is behind the mask, all clues,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:39.600
and recent LEGO releases, point to it being&nbsp;
T'Challa's sister, Shuri. The only question&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:43.920
is how she will handle the new role and the&nbsp;
throne that could potentially come with it.

00:03:43.920 --> 00:03:46.500
As Namor says at the beginning of the trailer,

00:03:46.500 --> 00:03:49.560
"Only the most broken people&nbsp;
can be great leaders,"

00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:55.380
Seems like with T'Challa gone, Shuri would fit the&nbsp;
bill. With that in mind, though, how long will it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.380 --> 00:04:00.300
be in the film before she steps into the role&nbsp;
and takes up the legendary mantle? And will it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:05.220
be enough to take on whoever's setting Atlantis&nbsp;
and Wakanda against each other? We'll have to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:10.620
wait and find out when "Black Panther: Wakanda&nbsp;
Forever" arrives in theaters on November 11.

